    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0513" n="409" xml:id="pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/118a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-20T17:00:00-05:00">February 20, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Reference Department’s February 5, 6 p.m. In response to a request received
                    from the Secretary of the Council of the League<anchor n="82" xml:id="d436-f1"/>
                    the Department desires that you continue to cooperate with the League Shanghai
                    Committee in preparing as soon as possible a report on present events. You
                    should follow the procedure indicated in the Department’s previous instruction
                    above referred to. Report action taken, and repeat to Nanking.</p>
                <p>Inform Minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
